#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-patch-id.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "git-patch-id(1)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-patch-id.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-patch-id.adoc:7
msgid "git-patch-id - Compute unique ID for a patch"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-patch-id.adoc:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-patch-id.adoc:12
msgid "git patch-id [--stable | --unstable | --verbatim]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-patch-id.adoc:14
#, no-wrap
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-patch-id.adoc:16
msgid "Read a patch from the standard input and compute the patch ID for it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-patch-id.adoc:21
msgid ""
"A \"patch ID\" is nothing but a sum of SHA-1 of the file diffs associated "
"with a patch, with line numbers ignored.  As such, it's \"reasonably "
"stable\", but at the same time also reasonably unique, i.e., two patches "
"that have the same \"patch ID\" are almost guaranteed to be the same thing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-patch-id.adoc:23
msgid "The main usecase for this command is to look for likely duplicate commits."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-patch-id.adoc:29
msgid ""
"When dealing with `git diff-tree` output, it takes advantage of the fact "
"that the patch is prefixed with the object name of the commit, and outputs "
"two 40-byte hexadecimal strings.  The first string is the patch ID, and the "
"second string is the commit ID.  This can be used to make a mapping from "
"patch ID to commit ID."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-patch-id.adoc:31
#, no-wrap
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-patch-id.adoc:33
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--verbatim`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-patch-id.adoc:36
msgid ""
"Calculate the patch-id of the input as it is given, do not strip any "
"whitespace."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-patch-id.adoc:38
msgid "This is the default if `patchid.verbatim` is `true`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-patch-id.adoc:39
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--stable`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-patch-id.adoc:41
msgid "Use a \"stable\" sum of hashes as the patch ID. With this option:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-patch-id.adoc:49
msgid ""
"Reordering file diffs that make up a patch does not affect the ID.  In "
"particular, two patches produced by comparing the same two trees with two "
"different settings for `-O<orderfile>` result in the same patch ID "
"signature, thereby allowing the computed result to be used as a key to index "
"some meta-information about the change between the two trees;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-patch-id.adoc:55
msgid ""
"Result is different from the value produced by git 1.9 and older or produced "
"when an \"unstable\" hash (see `--unstable` below) is configured - even when "
"used on a diff output taken without any use of `-O<orderfile>`, thereby "
"making existing databases storing such \"unstable\" or historical patch-ids "
"unusable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-patch-id.adoc:57
msgid "All whitespace within the patch is ignored and does not affect the id."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-patch-id.adoc:60
msgid "This is the default if `patchid.stable` is set to `true`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-patch-id.adoc:61
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--unstable`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-patch-id.adoc:67
msgid ""
"Use an \"unstable\" hash as the patch ID. With this option, the result "
"produced is compatible with the patch-id value produced by git 1.9 and older "
"and whitespace is ignored.  Users with pre-existing databases storing "
"patch-ids produced by git 1.9 and older (who do not deal with reordered "
"patches) may want to use this option."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-patch-id.adoc:69
msgid "This is the default."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-patch-id.adoc:71
#, no-wrap
msgid "GIT"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-patch-id.adoc:72
msgid "Part of the linkgit:git[1] suite"
msgstr ""
